==Trivia== 
* [[Professor Oak's Pokémon Live Caster]]: {{p|Venipede}}
* {{Ash}} and {{an|Iris}} narrate the preview for [[BW029|the next episode]].
* An instrumental version of {{so|Best Wishes!}} is used as background music during Ash and {{AP|Oshawott}}'s training session.
* The bottle cap Oshawott picks up when he is looking for his scalchop resembles the Kanto-Cola cap that [[James]] found in ''[[DP043|Malice in Wonderland!]]''.
* This episode features only four [[human]] characters, matching the record previously set by ''[[EP003|Ash Catches a Pokémon]]'', ''[[BW018|Sewaddle and Burgh in Pinwheel Forest!]]'', ''[[BW024|Emolga the Irresistible!]]'', and ''[[BW025|Emolga and the New Volt Switch!]]''. Three more ''[[Pokémon the Series: Black & White]]'' episodes, ''[[BW032|Facing Fear with Eyes Wide Open!]]'', ''[[BW055|Scraggy and the Demanding Gothita!]]'', and ''[[BW074|Battling the Leaf Thieves!]]'', would also later come to share this record.
** This record would be broken 331 episodes later by ''[[SM077|Guiding an Awakening!]]'', which features only three human characters.

===Errors===
* In the English dub, Ash erroneously refers to {{m|Razor Shell}} as "Shell Blade", the Japanese name of the move.

===Dub edits===
* A remixed instrumental version of {{so|Black and White}} is used as background music during Ash and Oshawott's training session in the place of the instrumental Best Wishes!.
* In the [[Pokémon in South Asia|Hindi]] dub, the Cilan's added line when Oshawott's Aqua Jet was not going right; "{{tt|Jana Tha Japan Par Pahuch Gaye China|Wanted to go to Japan but instead reached China}}", refers to [[Pokémon world in relation to the real world|a real world place]].

